    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d709">

                <pb facs="0593" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/11564.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Consul General Shanklin.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-21T05:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 21, 1914, 5 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Furnish aid to any Americans in need and urge all to leave Mexico. Canada
                    telegraphs that it is the intention of local Mexican authorities to take all
                    soldiers from Vera Cruz to City of Mexico and tear up track. Keep in touch with
                    Canada and act according to information received. In view of uncertainty of the
                    situation it is better to take no chances.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
